# Dev server

Aurin runs Haus in their own PowerShell: `npm run dev` on port 3000 while changing code, or the built app (`npm start`) on port 80 day to day. Leave that process alone.

If a server is needed to verify a change and one is already listening on port 3000 or 80, use it and do not start another. Do not run `npm run dev`, `next dev`, or `npm start`. If neither port is up, ask Aurin to start one.

A hook blocks `npm run dev` and `next dev`. Another hook stops anything left on ports 3001–3009 when the turn ends. Never touch port 3000 or port 80.
